— Family Payments","noes":41,"question":"John Madigan I move: That the Senate— (a) supports the 20th anniversary of the International Day of the Family, today 15 May 2014; (b) recognises families as the foundation of our society through which our society thrives and flourishes; (c) acknowledges families are entitled to receive tax benefits to compensate for the cost of raising children including the recognition of the need for horizontal tax equity for all families; and (d) calls on the Government to: (i) ensure that families with dependent children receive adequate financial recognition for the cost of raising children, and (ii) provide equal childcare funding for all children whether they are cared for by a parent in their home or through childcare places for parents who choose to return to work. Nick Xenophon by leave—I move: Omit subparagraph (d)(ii). I seek leave to make a short statement. John Hogg Leave is granted for one minute. Nick Xenophon I support what Senator Madigan is attempting to do here with this motion. I think it is a very worthy motion. I am concerned about subparagraph (d)(ii) as to the implications of equal childcare funding for all children, whether they are cared for by a parent in their home or through childcare places for parents who choose to return to work. I think that the concerns of Senator Madigan are expressed in particularly (c) and (d)(i) of the motion. I have some concerns—and it is not a criticism of Senator Madigan at all—as to what the implications would be of equal childcare funding and how that would work. But I think what Senator Madigan is trying to do is very important in acknowledging the role of families and their being entitled to receive tax benefits to compensate for the cost of raising children. John Hogg The question is that the amendment moved by Senator Xenophon be agreed to. Question agreed to. The question now is that the motion, as amended, be agreed to. Mitch Fifield I seek leave to make a short statement. John Hogg Leave is granted for one minute.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3204","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2014-05-15/2"}
